gin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.01704662622488423,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":8.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.679635103752107,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.0688034096112314,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":39.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.5261994499920184,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.14809939098760116,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":99.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.154684767391428,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.15646146278285622,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.04243055504678982,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":92.4,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.005457300355938145,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":17.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.05203749882623199,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0114559264646943,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.00253,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Royal Gold, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, acquires and manages precious metal streams, royalties, and related interests in North America, South and Central America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Australia Pacific. It operates through Acquisition and Management of Stream Interests and Acquisition and Management of Royalty Interests segments. The company engages in the acquisition of existing stream and royalty interests; and the financing of projects that are in production, development, or in the exploration stage in exchange for stream or royalty interests, which consists of gold, silver, copper, nickel, zinc, lead, molybdenum, diamonds, uranium, iron, platinum, palladium, rhodium, lithium, titanium, cobalt, barite, tungsten, and coal. Its properties are located in Canada, Chile, the Dominican Republic, the United States, Zambia, Australia, Ghana, Brazil, Mexico, Bolivia, Argentina, Nicaragua, Macedonia, Botswana, Spain, and internationally. Royal Gold, Inc. was incorporated in 1981 and is based in Denver, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William H. Heissenbuttel | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 39 people. Revenue per employee of $26.4M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $303K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Royal Gold, Inc. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $21.7B market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 54% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 33\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 4.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 369% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.689908147953113},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 53% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","25 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Gross margin tops the Basic Materials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (RGLD) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_RGLD_Volatility_111326072601_1